ca_body:"This fault has repeated {count} times within 60 days ({category}). The same temporary repair will not hold \u2014 apply the permanent fix:",rca_fix_media_converter:"Permanent fix: install a 12V mini-UPS for the media converter, or migrate this drop to a passive PLC splitter.",rca_fix_fiber_cut:"Permanent fix: re-route the exposed drop span through protective conduit and move the splice point off the exposed span, sealed inside a joint box.",rca_fix_fiber_splice_loss:"Permanent fix: re-splice with the fusion splicer, verify the RX reading at the customer end, and seal the joint in a proper splice closure box \u2014 no hand twists.",rca_fix_fiber_cut_splice:"Permanent fix: re-route the exposed span through protective conduit, fusion-splice the break, and seal the joint in a proper closure box.",rca_fix_router_config:"Permanent fix: save the working router settings on the customer profile, set a fixed IP / PPPoE plan, and replace the router if it keeps losing its configuration.",rca_fix_cat6_connector:"Permanent fix: replace the full CAT6 run with outdoor-grade cable and fresh RJ45 connectors at both ends instead of re-crimping the old ends.",rca_fix_wapda_power:"Permanent fix: install a 12V mini-UPS for the customer router / media converter so short WAPDA outages stop dropping the connection.",rca_fix_slow_speed:"Permanent fix: measure RX at the drop \u2014 if it is below -27 dBm, re-splice or move the customer to a closer splitter port; if RX is healthy, check the media converter and the LAN side.",prc_open_btn:"\u{1F91D} Post-Repair Check-Ins",prc_title:"Post-Repair Check-Ins",prc_intro:"Customers whose complaint was fixed 24\u201348 hours ago and have not been checked on yet. Send a 1-tap WhatsApp check-in to ask whether the connection is working fine now.",prc_summary_none:"No check-ins due right now.",prc_summary_count:"{count} customer(s) waiting for a check-in",prc_empty:"No complaints are in the 24\u201348 hour check-in window right now.",prc_field_cu